> Now that you kind folks have my elven Ranger wielding his bow, and he
> has cleaned out the quest, the castle, and Ludios, I have an
> observation I'd like the collected wisdom on.
>
> In past games, it seems to me that if a monster is carrying a potion of
> Gain Level they will quaff it after the first blow falls from my melee
> weapon. In this game, however, I've already taken 3 !oGL's off of arrow
> filled corpses, where it's taken two or three rounds of ranged combat
> to bring them down. This leads to my question - are monsters less
> likely to quaff their potions when they're being attacked from afar, or
> is it just the RNG being particularly kind to me this game?

The code in muse.c and monmove.c is difficult to read,
but it appears that monsters only use items when they
start attacking you.  They will use any offensive item
first, then any defensive item, then any misc item.
!oGL is a misc item.  So any monster will need to run
out of arrows and such before they start using up
defensive items and use up defensive items before using
up misc ones.

I suspect that the key in this is when you're doing
remote attacks on a monster, it's moving towards you
but has not yet come into range where it thinks it's
fighting you yet.  The farther you can shoot arrows, the
more often you'll be able to kill a monster before it
ever gets to the point that it decides to start attacking
you.  If it never decides to attack you, it never uses
up its items.

There's also the issue of death drops.  When monsters
die sometimes an item is created.  Since that item did
not exist in its inventory, it never could use it.  If
you end up killing a lot more monsters remotely, you'll
end up seeing more death drops from those corpses.


